      '# COMMUNITY VOLUME: SUBMISSIONS OPEN\n\n## Volume 7 Will Be Built By You\n\n![Open Submission](https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1517048676732-d65bc937f952?q=80&w=1000&auto=format&fit=crop)\n\nThe window is open. Between now and the end of June, we are accepting submissions for **Volume 7 — the community-created spatial volume**. Anything counts: a build you shipped, an essay on where AI is going, a tool you love, a lesson you learned the hard way.\n\n### The Rules, Kept Simple\n- **May–June:** Submit via the form on krackeddevs.com.\n- **June:** The community votes on shortlisted nodes.\n- **July:** The pipeline compiles the winners into Volume 7, with every contributor credited as co-author.\n\n### What Makes a Strong Node\nLook at what won this year\'s bounties: projects that were **local, practical, and shipped**. We want the same for the community volume — real builds and real perspectives over polish.\n\nThis is the project we started the year promising. It is the volume where the magazine finally practices what it preaches: **a network that writes its own story.**', 

